-- title:
--   Two-parameter local jet generators give exactly the summed-order differential ideal
-- statement:
--   For any ideal $I$ and nonnegative cutoffs $T,T'$, take the original homogeneous equations of $I$, their normalized jets of order at most $T'$ after translation by $g'$, and then their orbit derivatives of order at most $T$ after translation by $g$. Give each resulting section its genuine normalized coordinate domain at $g+g'+x$. The ideal locally generated by these two-parameter sections equals the intrinsic differential ideal at $g+g'$ with cutoff $T+T'$. Both inclusions hold as actual ideals, with regular rational coefficients in local expressions; multiplicities are retained. The proof identifies the individual sections on their domains and splits every direction list of length at most $T+T'$ into the two bounds. This statement does not assert that differentiating the entire inner locally generated ideal produces these sections; that is a separate local-generation step.
-- source:
--   Philippon (1986), Lemmes de zéros dans les groupes algébriques commutatifs, proof of Proposition 4.3, printed pp. 373–374, especially the two-parameter formula and the ideal generated by it on p. 374: https://numdam.org/articles/10.24033/bsmf.2060/ .

import Definitions.Def_PhilipponMultiplicity_IteratedJets
set_option autoImplicit false
open scoped BigOperators Topology
open PhilipponMultiplicity
attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable

theorem PhilipponMultiplicity.iterated_jet_sections_eq_differentialIdeal
    (K : Type*) [NontriviallyNormedField K] [CompleteSpace K]
    (G : EmbeddedGroupProduct K) (A : AnalyticSubgroup G)
    (g g' : G.Point) (T T' : ℕ) (I : Ideal G.CoordinateRing) :
    locallyGeneratedIdeal G (iteratedDifferentialSections A g g' T T' I) =
      differentialIdeal A (g+g') (T+T') I := by sorry
